{
  "_about": "The LLM-9 hostile-string corpus (LLM_ASSISTANT_SCOPE.md milestone LLM-9; security bar 3). Every row is a string that could reach the model (a Vault note, a faction or place name, a pasted request, a tool result) and the calls a model that FULLY OBEYED it would make. The Rust gate crates/cartalith-godot/tests/llm9_corpus.rs and the windowed probe godot-project/_llmquery_probe.gd run every row; the corpus only grows (the gate pins the id list below and a row count). Fields: id; family; text (the hostile string as it reaches the app; optional repeat_text multiplies it); legit_open (the setting groups the user's own request legitimately opened with get_param_schema before the string took effect); obey (one reply of tool calls the obedient model makes: {name, arguments}; a string in arguments of the form '@PADn' is replaced by n letters x); repeat (the obey reply is repeated this many times, default 1); reply_text (words the obedient model writes instead of calling anything); expect_rule (the validator rule the first obeyed proposal must hit, when it is a proposal); expect_valid (the exact keys that may be valid, when a proposal is expected to pass in part). Rows W01-W18 (LLM-6d) are VIEW-ACTION rows: their obey calls are propose_view_actions (and, in W14, set_generation_params in the same reply), the gate installs a view catalogue for every row, and expect_view_valid lists the exact action ids that may be valid. Rows K01-K24 and N01-N12 (RK-7, 2026-10-26) are KNOWLEDGE rows: `vector` says whether the text is a Vault note body (vault_note) or a world entity name (world_name); `crates/cartalith-godot/tests/rk7_knowledge_hardening.rs` plants each in a real Vault or world, retrieves it through the real index and the three knowledge tools, and checks what a model would be told. Nothing here is a real credential: every key-like string is FAKE.",
